evelopment, supports e4 or c6 ideas later.\n- P: e7-e5 — Also good, but d5 is more urgent given that it directly counters potential White central play via e4.\n\nReason: The move d7-d5 is the most assertive and strategically sound response. It fights for the center immediately, follows opening principles (control center, open lines for minor pieces), and does not weaken my position. It also prepares smooth development toward castling.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5"}
