ng queen.\n- **N: b8-c6 or N: b8-d7**: Developing knights, but again, misses the free queen.\n- **B: f8-g7 or B: f8-e6**: Developing the bishop, but slow compared to capturing a queen.\n- **K: e8-e7 or K: e8-d7**: King movement is unnecessary when material can be won.\n\nReason: Capturing the undefended white queen with **Q: d8-d5** is the most forcing and advantageous move. It wins a full queen for no cost, dramatically improving Black's position. There is no threat to the black queen after capture (no pawn or piece defends d5), so the capture is safe. This move maximizes winning chances by securing decisive material advantage.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-d5"}
