ns **Q: d5-a2+** — because it gives check and forces the white king to move, likely losing castling rights (though already lost) and exposing it.\n\nAfter Qa2+, Kc1, then I can play Nc6, developing with tempo.\n\nBut is there a better check?\n\n**Q: d5-c4+**? c4 is not on the same file/rank/diagonal as d1? d5 to c4 is -1,-1 — diagonal, but c4 to d1 is +1,-3 — not aligned. So not check.\n\nOnly checks from queen are those that land on squares attacking d1.\n\nd1 is on d-file, 1st rank, and diagonals a4-d1, h5-d1, etc.\n\nSquares from which queen can check d1:\n\n- Any on d-file except d1: d2,d3,d4,d5,d6,d7,d8\n- Any on 1st rank: a1,b1,c1,e1,f1,g1,h1\n- Diagonals: a4,b3,c2,e2,f3,g4,h5 (for a4-d1); and h4,g3,f2,e1 (for h4-d1)\n\nFrom d5, queen can go to:\n\n- d2, d3, d4, d6, d7, d8 — all on d-file — any of these would be check if empty and not blocked.\n\nIs d2 blocked? d2 has BWF1 (white bishop), so queen cannot go to d2.\n\nd3: empty? Board shows d3 is empty — yes.\n\nd4: has PBF1 (black pawn) — so blocked.\n\nSo queen cannot go to d3 or d4 because d4 is occupied by my own pawn.\n\nPath from d5 to d3: must pass through d4, which has my pawn — so I cannot jump — so Qd5-d3 is illegal.\n\nSimilarly, d5 to d2: passes through d4 and d3 — d4 blocked.\n\nSo no d-file checks.\n\nRank 1: can queen reach e1? d5 to e1: +1,-4 — not straight. Only if diagonal or orthogonal.\n\ne1 is on same diagonal? d5 to e1: +1,-4 — no, not diagonal (would need equal delta).\n\nClosest diagonal: from d5, diagonals are:\n\n- a8-g2 direction: c6,b7,a8\n- h1-a8 direction: e4,f3,g2,h1 — yes! d5-e4-f3-g2-h1\n\nSo queen can go to h1, g2, f3, e4 on that diagonal.\n\nh1: empty? Yes.\n\ng2: has BBF1 (my bishop) — so blocked.\n\nSo queen can go to e4, f3, h1 — but not beyond g2.\n\nCan it check the king on d1 from any of these?\n\n- From e4: e4 to d1 is -1,-3 — not orthogonal or diagonal. No.\n- From f3: f3 to d1 is -2,-2 — yes! Diagonal. So if queen is on f3, it attacks d1.\n\nAnd f3 is empty.\n\nAnd pa